#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Ferry: a mailbox between your devices, over Tailscale. This is a Linux computer's side of it.

    ferry send [FILE…|TEXT]       files, or a text; with nothing: what is piped in, or the clipboard (--to DEVICE: see below)
    ferry list                    what's in the box, numbered: what was received (1 is the newest), then what was sent
    ferry get [N]                 an item (1, the newest received, by default): a text printed, a file copied here
    ferry open | copy N           a file opened, a text to the clipboard
    ferry rm N…                   items out of the box (a received file stays in Downloads)
    ferry clear [received|sent]   everything, or one direction, out of the box
    ferry url | qr                the phone's address (https://<this machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net/ferry/), or Add Device's QR code
    ferry status                  on, or off and why (the server not running)
    ferry enable | disable        the server on/off (ferry.service) and its address on the tailnet
    ferry run                     the server itself (the service)
    ferry app [FILE…]             Ferry's window (files: sends them, after picking the device); --background: the tray
    ferry update [--check]        installs Ferry's newest release (a beta install: the newest pre-release too)
    ferry tray [on|off]           whether the tray icon starts at login (`ferry enable` puts it there)
    ferry version                 this Ferry's version
    ferry list --json             the box and Ferry's state, for a desktop's menu
    ferry qr --svg                the QR code as an SVG file (prints its path), for the menu
    ferry add FILE…               sends files (or a folder's files) without a word (the menu's drop)
    ferry pick                    the same, files chosen in a file dialog (several at once); then the menu says "Sent"
    ferry text TEXT               sends a text
    ferry send-clipboard          sends the clipboard's text (a notification if it has none); to a computer, onto its clipboard
    ferry devices                 the owner's other devices (computers running Ferry, phones that used it), the picked one marked
    ferry target [DEVICE]         the device sends go to (the last one picked), or picks one
    ferry forget DEVICE           a device off every computer's and phone's lists, until it is added again
    ferry seen                    marks what came from the phone as seen (the bar's count goes)
    N is a number from `ferry list`, or an item's id (the menu uses those: numbers change as the box does).
    send, add, pick, text and send-clipboard take --to DEVICE (its name in `ferry devices`) for one send, else the target.

Either end leaves files or text in the box, and they wait there until the other end picks them up. The phone needs no
app: a web page served by this script, which it can add to its Home Screen (a PWA with Web Push notifications). The
devices don't have to be on the same network, only on the same tailnet.

The server listens on localhost only. `tailscale serve` publishes it on the tailnet at MOUNT with the tailnet's real
certificate (iOS writes to the clipboard and allows a PWA and Web Push only on HTTPS), and tells it who is asking: a
request is answered only for the Tailscale user who owns this machine (Tailscale-User-Login, which tailscale serve sets
and a client can't). A custom header on every API call keeps other web pages on the phone from posting here (their
cross-site request would need a CORS preflight, which isn't answered).

Every send goes to one device. For a phone it waits in this computer's box, marked for that phone ("for"): only that
phone's page lists it (the page asks every computer, and each answers with what is for the device asking) and only it
gets the notification. For another computer it goes straight there, as the phone's page sends: it lands in that
computer's box and menu, and Send Clipboard onto its clipboard. The server keeps the owner's computers that answer as
Ferry in STATE/machines.json for the commands and the menu (`ferry devices`).

Several computers: each runs its own Ferry, and the page shows them as one. It asks its own computer which of the owner's
other machines answer at MOUNT (/api/machines), lists what all of them hold, and sends to the one picked above the form,
talking to each directly: a computer answers another one's page (CORS) only if that one belongs to the same owner. A phone's push
subscription belongs to the computer it added the page from, so the others ask that one to pass their notifications on
(/api/relay, /api/relay-push).

A request must name this machine (Host: its tailnet name), so a web page that rebinds its own name to 127.0.0.1 in a
browser here gets nothing. Anyone logged in to this computer could still reach the local port with made-up headers:
Ferry trusts the computer's own users, as a single-user desktop does.

Kept in STATE: items.json (the box), the files left for the phone (files/), the VAPID key for Web Push (made on the first
run; python3-cryptography), the phone's push subscriptions, the phones that have used Ferry here (phones.json: the
device list shows only those) and the devices the owner forgot (forgotten.json, which reaches the other computers
through api/ping). Files from the phone go to Downloads. Items go after
KEEP_DAYS days, a code or a password after SECRET_KEEP or once copied; removing one from the box doesn't delete a file in
Downloads. Nightdrive's Ferry plugin, where this
server came from, kept the same state in OLD_STATE: the first run moves it here (migrate()).

The desktop: the service starts with the user's session, maybe before the desktop, so the desktop's variables (Wayland's
or X11's display) are looked up whenever the clipboard or a notification needs them (desktop_env()). The clipboard is
wl-clipboard's, or xclip's on X11 and where Wayland's can't be reached; notifications go over a session bus connection
of the process's own, through PyGObject, which hears their buttons pressed (Notifications), else they are notify-send's;
how long the computer has been idle comes from the compositor, Mutter, X11 or logind (idle_for()). A desktop's own Ferry
menu hears about changes through HOOK, run with the event's name ("changed": the box or a send; "picked": files sent
from `ferry pick`'s dialog).
"""
import contextlib
import fcntl
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request

# The package beside bin/: ~/.local/bin/ferry is a link to bin/ferry, so the real path
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))))
from ferry import computers, config, desktop, forget, notices, push, server, store, tailnet, terminal  # noqa: E402


def version_key(v):
    """1.0.0-beta.2 sorts before 1.0.0, which sorts before 1.0.1-beta.1."""
    base, _, pre = v.lstrip("v").partition("-")
    nums = tuple(int(n) for n in re.findall(r"\d+", base)[:3])
    return nums + ((0, int((re.findall(r"\d+", pre) or ["0"])[-1])) if pre else (1, 0))


def is_beta(v=None):
    """A beta install is one running a pre-release: it follows pre-releases, until it updates to a full release."""
    return "-" in (config.VERSION if v is None else v)


def newest_release(releases, beta):
    """The newest release with Linux files (GitHub's releases API's list), pre-releases only for a beta:
    {version, tag, tarball, script}, or None."""
    found = []
    for r in releases:
        if r.get("draft") or (r.get("prerelease") and not beta):
            continue
        assets = {a.get("name"): a.get("browser_download_url") for a in r.get("assets") or []}
        if assets.get(config.TARBALL) and assets.get("install.sh"):
            tag = r.get("tag_name", "")
            found.append({"version": tag.lstrip("v"), "tag": tag, "tarball": assets[config.TARBALL],
                          "script": assets["install.sh"]})
    return max(found, key=lambda r: version_key(r["version"]), default=None)


def fetch_releases():
    req = urllib.request.Request(config.RELEASES, headers={"Accept": "application/vnd.github+json",
                                                    "User-Agent": f"Ferry/{config.VERSION}"})
    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:
        return json.load(r)


def check_update(fetch=fetch_releases, max_age=None):
    """A release newer than this Ferry, or None; asks GitHub unless it was asked in the last max_age seconds. The
    answer is kept in STATE/update.json for available_update(). A failed check raises (OSError, ValueError)."""
    path = os.path.join(config.STATE, "update.json")
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            cached = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        cached = {}
    if max_age is None or time.time() - cached.get("checked", 0) > max_age:
        latest = newest_release(fetch(), is_beta())
        cached = {"checked": time.time(), "latest": latest}
        os.makedirs(config.STATE, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
        with open(path + ".tmp", "w") as f:
            json.dump(cached, f)
        os.replace(path + ".tmp", path)
    return available_update(cached)


def available_update(cached=None):
    """The last check's newer release, without asking GitHub."""
    if cached is None:
        try:
            with open(os.path.join(config.STATE, "update.json")) as f:
                cached = json.load(f)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            return None
    latest = cached.get("latest")
    return latest if latest and version_key(latest["version"]) > version_key(config.VERSION) else None


def update(check_only=False):
    """`ferry update`: the newer release's own install script, run with that release's files, as a first install
    does (the packages it needs, the service restarted)."""
    try:
        new = check_update()
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        print(f"Couldn't check for updates: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    if not new:
        print(f"Ferry {config.VERSION} is the latest" + (" (beta)" if is_beta() else ""))
        return 0
    if check_only:
        print(f"Ferry {new['version']} is out: ferry update installs it")
        return 0
    print(f"Updating Ferry {config.VERSION} to {new['version']}", flush=True)
    tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp()
    try:
        script = os.path.join(tmp, "install.sh")
        req = urllib.request.Request(new["script"], headers={"User-Agent": f"Ferry/{config.VERSION}"})
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as r, open(script, "wb") as f:
            shutil.copyfileobj(r, f)
        env = dict(os.environ, FERRY_DOWNLOAD_URL=new["tarball"])
        return subprocess.run(["bash", script] + (["--beta"] if is_beta(new["version"]) else []), env=env).returncode
    except OSError as e:
        print(f"Couldn't download the update: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(tmp, ignore_errors=True)


def quietly(*cmd):
    with contextlib.suppress(OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        subprocess.run(cmd, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, timeout=30)


def desktop_entry(background=False):
    """Ferry's .desktop file: the window in the app list, and "Open With → Ferry" for any file, which sends it; or
    (background) the tray icon, started at login. It runs this copy of ferry."""
    exe = os.path.join(config.ROOT, "bin", "ferry")
    exe = f'"{exe}"' if re.search(r"[\s\"'\\]", exe) else exe
    lines = ["[Desktop Entry]", "Type=Application", "Name=Ferry", "GenericName=Device Mailbox",
             "Comment=Send texts, the clipboard and files to your other devices over Tailscale",
             f"Icon={config.APP_ID}", "Terminal=false"]
    if background:
        lines += [f"Exec={exe} app --background", "NoDisplay=true", "X-GNOME-Autostart-enabled=true"]
    else:
        lines += [f"Exec={exe} app %F", "Categories=Network;FileTransfer;Utility;",
                  "Keywords=send;share;clipboard;phone;iPhone;Tailscale;",
                  # Open With for any file in KDE, which takes every type as a kind of application/octet-stream. Not
                  # the types themselves: a desktop file in the user's own folder would become their default app
                  # (GNOME's PDFs would open Ferry); the file managers' own menus have "Send with Ferry" instead
                  "MimeType=application/octet-stream;", "StartupNotify=true", "SingleMainWindow=true"]
    return "\n".join(lines) + "\n"


def write_file(path, text):
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
    with open(path + ".tmp", "w") as f:
        f.write(text)
    os.replace(path + ".tmp", path)


def file_manager_menus():
    """"Send with Ferry" in the file managers' own menus, for the selected files: {path: (text, executable)}. GNOME
    Files has it under Scripts, Dolphin (KDE) and Nemo (Cinnamon) in the menu itself."""
    exe = os.path.join(config.ROOT, "bin", "ferry")
    quoted = f'"{exe}"' if re.search(r"[\s\"'\\]", exe) else exe
    data, home = config.data_home(), os.path.expanduser("~")
    return {
        os.path.join(data, "nautilus", "scripts", "Send with Ferry"):
            (f'#!/bin/sh\n# Ferry\'s "Send with Ferry" in GNOME Files (Scripts): the selected files, after picking the device\n'
             f'exec "{exe}" app "$@"\n', True),
        os.path.join(data, "kio", "servicemenus", config.APP_ID + ".desktop"):
            ("[Desktop Entry]\nType=Service\nMimeType=all/allfiles;\nActions=send;\nX-KDE-Priority=TopLevel\n\n"
             f"[Desktop Action send]\nName=Send with Ferry\nIcon={config.APP_ID}\nExec={quoted} app %F\n", True),
        os.path.join(data, "nemo", "actions", "ferry.nemo_action"):
            ("[Nemo Action]\nName=Send with Ferry\nComment=Send the selected files to one of your devices\n"
             f"Exec={quoted} app %F\nIcon-Name={config.APP_ID}\nSelection=notnone\nExtensions=nodirs;\n", False),
    }


def install_launcher():
    """Ferry in the app list and the file managers' menus, its icon, and its tray icon at login unless
    `ferry tray off`."""
    write_file(os.path.join(config.APPLICATIONS, config.APP_ID + ".desktop"), desktop_entry())
    for path, (text, executable) in file_manager_menus().items():
        write_file(path, text)
        if executable:   # Dolphin runs a service menu only if it is
            os.chmod(path, 0o755)
    for size in (192, 512):
        d = os.path.join(config.ICONS, f"{size}x{size}", "apps")
        os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
        shutil.copyfile(os.path.join(config.WEB, f"icon-{size}.png"), os.path.join(d, config.APP_ID + ".png"))
    set_tray(tray_wanted())
    quietly("update-desktop-database", config.APPLICATIONS)
    quietly("gtk-update-icon-cache", "-q", "-t", config.ICONS)


def tray_wanted():
    return not os.path.exists(config.NO_TRAY)


def set_tray(on):
    """The tray icon at login, or not (remembered across updates)."""
    path = os.path.join(config.AUTOSTART, config.APP_ID + ".desktop")
    if on:
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.remove(config.NO_TRAY)
        write_file(path, desktop_entry(background=True))
    else:
        write_file(config.NO_TRAY, "")
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.remove(path)


def listing():
    st = tailnet.tailscale_status()
    with store.box() as items:
        out = [dict(store.public(i), path=i.get("path", "")) for i in items]
    subs = push.subscriptions() if os.path.exists(os.path.join(config.STATE, "push.json")) else []
    devs = computers.devices(st)
    t = computers.target(devs)
    on = tailnet.systemctl("is-active", "-q", config.SERVICE).returncode == 0
    have = bool(shutil.which("tailscale"))
    served = have and bool(st) and tailnet.serving()
    return {"on": on, "tailscale": st.get("BackendState") == "Running", "url": tailnet.url(st), "serving": served,
            "setup": tailnet.setup_step(st, have, on, served), "push": len(subs), "items": out, "devices": devs,
            "target": t["id"] if t else "", "sent": computers.last_sent(), "version": config.VERSION, "update": available_update()}


def add_link(u):
    """What Add Device's QR code holds for the address `u` (docs/protocol.md › Clients › Adding a phone)."""
    return f"{config.ADD_PAGE}#{u}" if u else ""


def qr(svg):
    u = tailnet.url()
    if not u or not shutil.which("qrencode"):
        print("No address: Tailscale is off" if not u else "qrencode is needed: install it with your package manager",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    if not svg:
        return subprocess.run(["qrencode", "-t", "ANSIUTF8", "-m", "2", add_link(u)]).returncode
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(config.QR), exist_ok=True)
    subprocess.run(["qrencode", "-t", "SVG", "-m", "2", "--foreground=000000", "--background=FFFFFF", "-o", config.QR,
                    add_link(u)], check=True)
    print(config.QR)
    return 0


def install_unit():
    """The unit into the user's units, its ExecStart naming this copy of ferry (the installed one, or a checkout's)."""
    with open(config.UNIT) as f:
        unit = f.read()
    exe = os.path.realpath(__file__).replace("%", "%%")
    exe = f'"{exe}"' if re.search(r"\s", exe) else exe
    unit = re.sub(r"(?m)^ExecStart=.*$", lambda _: f"ExecStart={exe} run", unit)
    os.makedirs(config.USER_UNITS, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = os.path.join(config.USER_UNITS, config.SERVICE + ".tmp")
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        f.write(unit)
    os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(config.USER_UNITS, config.SERVICE))


def enable():
    """The server on: its unit installed and (re)started, so an update runs the new copy, published on the tailnet,
    and the app in the desktop's app list."""
    if not push.vapid_key(create=True):
        print("No python3-cryptography: Ferry works, but without notifications on the phone", file=sys.stderr)
    stop_old()   # its port is this one's
    install_unit()
    install_launcher()
    tailnet.systemctl("daemon-reload")
    for args in (("enable", config.SERVICE), ("restart", config.SERVICE)):
        res = tailnet.systemctl(*args)
        if res.returncode:
            print(res.stderr.strip() or f"systemctl --user {' '.join(args)} failed", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
    if not shutil.which("tailscale"):
        print("Ferry is on, and needs Tailscale to be reached: https://tailscale.com/download/linux, then: ferry enable",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    err = tailnet.serve(True)
    if err:
        print(tailnet.serve_message(err), file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    print(tailnet.url() or "Ferry is on; Tailscale is off, so the page has no address yet")
    return 0


def stop_old():
    """Nightdrive's Ferry plugin's server, off for good: this one takes its port and its state."""
    tailnet.systemctl("disable", "--now", config.OLD_SERVICE)


def migrate(old=config.OLD_STATE, new=config.STATE, stop=stop_old):
    """Moves the state of Nightdrive's Ferry plugin here, once: the VAPID key the phones' subscriptions are bound to,
    the subscriptions, the computers found and the box, so the phones keep their notifications and the box its items.
    True when it moved.

    Under a lock on new's parent folder, so that two commands starting at once neither both move it nor one makes a new
    state (and a new VAPID key) while the other moves the old. The box's paths to files left for the phone are rewritten
    before the move, so no reader ever finds them gone (a write drops items whose file is gone)."""
    if os.path.exists(new) or not os.path.isdir(old):
        return False
    parent = os.path.dirname(new)
    os.makedirs(parent, exist_ok=True)
    fd = os.open(parent, os.O_RDONLY)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        if os.path.exists(new) or not os.path.isdir(old):
            return False
        stop()
        path = os.path.join(old, "items.json")
        try:
            with open(path) as f:
                data = json.load(f)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            data = None
        if isinstance(data, dict) and isinstance(data.get("items"), list):
            for it in data["items"]:
                p = it.get("path") if isinstance(it, dict) else None
                if isinstance(p, str) and p.startswith(old + os.sep):
                    it["path"] = new + p[len(old):]
            with open(path + ".tmp", "w") as f:
                json.dump(data, f, ensure_ascii=False)
            os.replace(path + ".tmp", path)
        try:
            os.rename(old, new)
        except OSError:   # on another file system
            shutil.copytree(old, new, symlinks=True)
            shutil.rmtree(old)
        os.chmod(new, 0o700)
        return True
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


def main():
    a = sys.argv[1:]
    cmd = a[0] if a else "status"
    try:
        if cmd not in ("version", "--version", "help", "-h", "--help") and migrate():
            print(f"Ferry's state moved from {config.OLD_STATE} to {config.STATE}", file=sys.stderr)
    except OSError as e:   # nothing may start over with a new state (and VAPID key) beside a half-moved one
        print(f"Couldn't move Ferry's state from {config.OLD_STATE} to {config.STATE}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    if cmd == "status":
        print(tailnet.status())
    elif cmd == "enable":
        return enable()
    elif cmd == "disable":
        tailnet.systemctl("disable", "--now", config.SERVICE)
        err = tailnet.serve(False)
        if err:
            print(tailnet.serve_message(err), file=sys.stderr)
    elif cmd == "run":
        server.run()
    elif cmd == "app":
        sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(config.ROOT, "app"))
        import ferry_app
        return ferry_app.main(sys.modules[__name__], a[1:])
    elif cmd == "update" and a[1:] in ([], ["--check"]):
        return update(check_only=a[1:] == ["--check"])
    elif cmd == "tray" and a[1:] in ([], ["on"], ["off"]):
        if len(a) == 1:
            print("on" if tray_wanted() else "off")
        else:
            set_tray(a[1] == "on")
    elif cmd in ("version", "--version"):
        print(config.VERSION)
    elif cmd == "url":
        u = tailnet.url()
        print(u)
        return 0 if u else 1
    elif cmd == "list" and a[1:] == ["--json"]:
        print(json.dumps(listing(), ensure_ascii=False))
    elif cmd == "list":
        terminal.print_list()
    elif cmd in ("send", "add", "pick", "text", "send-clipboard"):
        dev, rest, why = terminal.pick_device(a[1:])
        if not dev:
            # A device named with --to that isn't there is that, not "no device yet"
            if cmd == "send":
                print(why, file=sys.stderr)
                return 1
            return terminal.failed(why)
        if cmd == "send":
            return terminal.send(rest, dev)
        if cmd == "add":
            if not rest:
                return 1
            err = computers.deliver(dev, files=rest)
            return terminal.failed(err) if err else 0
        if cmd == "pick":
            paths = terminal.pick_files(f"Send to {dev['name']} with Ferry")
            if paths is None:
                return terminal.failed("No file dialog here (zenity or kdialog): ferry send FILE sends files")
            if not paths:
                return 1
            err = computers.deliver(dev, files=paths)
            # A menu that closed for the dialog may open again to show what was just sent
            desktop.hook("picked")
            return terminal.failed(err) if err else 0
        if cmd == "text":
            if not " ".join(rest).strip():
                return 1
            err = computers.deliver(dev, text=" ".join(rest))
            return terminal.failed(err) if err else 0
        text = desktop.paste_text()
        if not text.strip():
            notices.notify("The clipboard has no text", "Copy a text or a link first")
            computers.mark_sent("", "", "The clipboard has no text")
            return 1
        err = computers.deliver(dev, text=text, clip=True)
        return terminal.failed(err) if err else 0
    elif cmd == "devices":
        devs = computers.devices()
        t = computers.target(devs)
        for d in devs:
            state = "in use" if d["inUse"] else "online" if d["online"] else \
                "asleep" if d["kind"] == "computer" else "offline"
            print(f"{'*' if t and d['id'] == t['id'] else ' '} {d['id']:<24} {d['kind']:<9} {state}" +
                  (f"  ({d['name']})" if d["name"] != d["id"] else ""))
        if not devs:
            print("No other device yet: add your phone with Add Device in Ferry's menu (or ferry qr)", file=sys.stderr)
    elif cmd == "forget" and len(a) == 2:
        dev = next((d for d in computers.devices() if a[1] in (d["id"], d["name"])), None)
        if not dev:
            print(f"No device {a[1]}: see ferry devices", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        forget.decide(dev["id"], True)
    elif cmd == "target":
        devs = computers.devices()
        if len(a) == 1:
            t = computers.target(devs)
            print(t["id"] if t else "")
            return 0 if t else 1
        dev = next((d for d in devs if a[1] in (d["id"], d["name"])), None)
        if not dev:
            print(f"No device {a[1]}: see ferry devices", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        computers.set_target(dev["id"])
    elif cmd == "get" and len(a) <= 2:
        it = store.item(a[1] if len(a) > 1 else "1")
        if not it or (len(a) == 1 and it.get("to") != "computer"):
            print("Nothing from the phone" if len(a) == 1 else f"No item {a[1]}: see ferry list", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        return terminal.get(it)
    elif cmd in ("copy", "open", "rm", "remove") and len(a) > 1:
        items = store.numbered()
        found = [store.item(r, items) for r in a[1:]]   # all first: numbers would change as items go
        if None in found:
            print(f"No item {a[1 + found.index(None)]}: see ferry list", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        for it in found:
            if cmd in ("rm", "remove"):
                store.remove(it["id"])
            elif cmd == "copy" and it.get("kind") == "text":
                if not desktop.copy_text(it["text"], sensitive=store.secret(it)):
                    print("No clipboard to copy to: this needs a desktop", file=sys.stderr)
                    return 1
                store.copied(it)
            elif cmd == "open" and it.get("kind") == "file":
                desktop.open_path(it["path"])
            else:
                print(f"{'Copy' if cmd == 'copy' else 'Open'} is for a {'text' if cmd == 'copy' else 'file'}: "
                      f"ferry get {a[1 + found.index(it)]}", file=sys.stderr)
                return 1
        if cmd in ("rm", "remove"):
            desktop.changed()
    elif cmd == "clear" and len(a) <= 2:
        to = {"": None, "received": "computer", "sent": "phone"}.get(a[1] if len(a) > 1 else "", "?")
        if to == "?":
            print("ferry clear [received|sent]", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        with store.box(write=True) as items:
            for it in [i for i in items if to is None or i.get("to") == to]:
                store.drop_file(it)
                items.remove(it)
        desktop.changed()
    elif cmd == "seen":
        store.mark_seen()
    elif cmd == "qr":
        return qr(a[1:] == ["--svg"])
    elif cmd in ("help", "-h", "--help"):
        print(__doc__.split("\n\n")[1])
    else:
        print(__doc__.split("\n\n")[1], file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    return 0

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
